notes:
Put the list in the main pane and the record in the aside. The nav pane is too narrow for a table (it is for a tree or a list of sections). The route is the only state: a record active means `aside-open`, `active-pane="aside"`, `aside-label` set to the record's name and `current-row` set to its id; no record means the list alone. A row click, Back, Close, Cancel and Save only change the route, and a handler sets the properties from it, so a deep link, a refresh and the back button all land in the same place. On a phone the workspace shows one pane at a time with a tab strip (list, record): the record is its own page, and the header's back arrow (shown below 641px only) returns to the list. A tap on the list tab raises a cancelable `pk-pane-change`: the page vetoes it with `preventDefault()` and changes the route, which is how a host that owns `active-pane` keeps the route and the pane in step. The aside has no header of its own: build one from `pk-toolbar` (heading = the record's name, Back and Close in its `actions` slot).

In Blazor the same page is a `@page` component over `PkWorkspace` and `PkTable` (`CurrentRow`), with the route as the only state:

```razor
@page "/things"
@page "/things/{Id}"
@inject NavigationManager Nav

<PkWorkspace Fill MainLabel="Things" AsideLabel="@_title" AsideOpen="@_open" ActivePane="@_pane" OnPaneChange="PaneChanged">
    <PkStack Gap="sm">
        <PkToolbar Heading="Things" />
        <PkTable Items="_things" Columns="_columns" IdOf="t => t.Id" Label="Things" Clickable CurrentRow="@Id" OnRowClick="Open" />
    </PkStack>
    <AsideContent>
        <PkStack Gap="sm">
            <PkToolbar Heading="@_title">
                <ActionsContent>
                    <PkButton Size="ButtonSize.Mini" Variant="ButtonVariant.Ghost" OnClick="Close">Back</PkButton>
                </ActionsContent>
            </PkToolbar>
            <PkForm Summary OnValid="Close">
                <form @onsubmit:preventDefault>
                    <PkField Label="Name" Required><PkInput @bind-Value="_name" Name="name" Required /></PkField>
                    <PkFormActions Align="end">
                        <PkButton Type="button" Variant="ButtonVariant.Plain" OnClick="Close">Cancel</PkButton>
                        <PkButton Type="submit" Variant="ButtonVariant.Primary">Save</PkButton>
                    </PkFormActions>
                </form>
            </PkForm>
        </PkStack>
    </AsideContent>
</PkWorkspace>

@code {
    [Parameter] public string? Id { get; set; }

    private readonly List<Thing> _things = [new("1", "Blue widget"), new("2", "Red widget")];
    private readonly IReadOnlyList<PkTableColumn<Thing>> _columns = [new() { Key = "name", Label = "Name" }];
    private Thing? _thing;
    private string? _name;
    private string _title = "Thing";
    private string _pane = "main";
    private bool _open;

    // The route is the only state: it says which record is open, and this handler derives everything else from it.
    protected override void OnParametersSet()
    {
        _thing = _things.FirstOrDefault(t => t.Id == Id);
        _name = _thing?.Name;
        _title = _thing?.Name ?? "Thing";
        _open = _thing is not null;
        _pane = _open ? "aside" : "main";
    }

    private void Open(PkTableRowClickArgs<Thing> row) => Nav.NavigateTo($"/things/{row.Id}");
    private void Close() => Nav.NavigateTo("/things");
    private void PaneChanged(PkPaneChangeEventArgs e) { if (e.Pane == "main") Close(); }

    private record Thing(string Id, string Name);
}
```
